                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "b8248dd5-4a91-40b4-8c22-985c57888977",
                        "entry_id": "870d4def-1801-374c-a0f3-754ee592bef5",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "critériums"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "a4e7931c-1133-44fe-9867-dd5697451218",
                        "entry_id": "870d4def-1801-374c-a0f3-754ee592bef5",
                        "tags": [
                            "Plus rare"
                        ],
                        "form": "criterium"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ffedefea-31da-3450-ae27-3980989795e1",
                        "entry_id": "870d4def-1801-374c-a0f3-754ee592bef5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Preuve qu’une chose est telle qu’elle doit être, critère."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3d4c5c5a-fdae-435b-9548-46ac3241db59",
                                "sense_id": "ffedefea-31da-3450-ae27-3980989795e1",
                                "text": "La faculté de comprendre ou l’impossibilité de comprendre, dit fort judicieusement M. Mill, ne peut, dans aucun cas, être considérée comme un critérium de Vérité axiomatique."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "592fdf38-d33a-40bf-93c0-0120fed40670",
                                "sense_id": "ffedefea-31da-3450-ae27-3980989795e1",
                                "text": "Son interprétation rationnelle du symbolisme scripturaire s’exerce sans critérium ni règles fixes d’herméneutique pour distinguer ce qui, dans l’Écriture, doit être pris au sens littéral ou au figuré."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "12735045-4a26-40d3-802c-3467340607b8",
                                "sense_id": "ffedefea-31da-3450-ae27-3980989795e1",
                                "text": "Le bonheur que les utilitaristes ont adopté comme critérium de la moralité de la conduite n’est pas le bonheur personnel de l’agent, mais celui de tous les intéressés."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c8d52b43-a3cb-4921-968c-757cbfeab397",
                                "sense_id": "ffedefea-31da-3450-ae27-3980989795e1",
                                "text": "On était enclin déjà, je pense, à juger la qualité et la compétence d’un médecin par le prix qu’il fait payer : plus il prend cher, et plus il doit être savant. Ce critérium s’applique encore davantage aux médicastres, aux voyantes et aux charlatans."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b8a36559-7d36-43b4-94e3-5aaead10439e",
                                "sense_id": "ffedefea-31da-3450-ae27-3980989795e1",
                                "text": "Marie ne peut rester cinq minutes sans aller admirer sa corbeille. Elle prend un plaisir extrême à entendre le craquement de ses bottines neuves. Pour elle, ce bruit est le critérium de l’élégance."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7ca73f16-085c-4583-865b-7cebf9df86b8",
                        "source_entry_id": "870d4def-1801-374c-a0f3-754ee592bef5",
                        "source_sense_id": "ffedefea-31da-3450-ae27-3980989795e1",
                        "target_lang_word": "criterion",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "criterion",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d1c135db-69bd-3167-8d5b-ed9657c215ec",
                                        "entry_id": "ffb853b8-ec97-3fe2-acdd-532dceab032a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A standard, test, or requirement by which individual things or people may be compared and judged; a gauge."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6d64ee4-c169-408a-a6eb-cbf2b880dc57",
                                                "sense_id": "d1c135db-69bd-3167-8d5b-ed9657c215ec",
                                                "text": "Near-synonym: benchmark"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "abe42da4-0823-4156-a9cf-41e17b46746d",
                                                "sense_id": "d1c135db-69bd-3167-8d5b-ed9657c215ec",
                                                "text": "criterion of choice, of decision, of selection"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2bb4ec4d-bccd-462f-90db-2790fc4062f8",
                                                "sense_id": "d1c135db-69bd-3167-8d5b-ed9657c215ec",
                                                "text": "Knowledge has come to her too soon—knowledge of evil, unqualified by the general charities which longer experience infallibly brings; but her age has lent its own freshness to this first great emotion; it becomes unconsciously a criterion, and the judgment is harsh, because the remembrance is bitter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9bea3d50-1594-438c-808c-21887d4528ff",
                                                "sense_id": "d1c135db-69bd-3167-8d5b-ed9657c215ec",
                                                "text": "The Enlightment worldview, which considered the order of \"Nature\" as a basis and, at the same time, the subject of explorations of scientific natural sciences, has, at the same time, considered this order as a criterion of the artistically-aesthetic qualities of art. From an \"ideological\" point of view, it liberated art from its feudal religious and courtly servitude."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48936ab0-fb2b-4eea-b0e4-96429614dc55",
                                                "sense_id": "d1c135db-69bd-3167-8d5b-ed9657c215ec",
                                                "text": "Congratulations on managing to use the phrase “preponderant criterion” in a chart (“On your marks”, November 9th). Was this the work of a kakorrhaphiophobic journalist set a challenge by his colleagues, or simply an example of glossolalia?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
